[b]The Stack as Queer Memory[/b]

The **[ and ]** operations (push/pop stack) enable something profound:

**You can explore alternate timelines and return.**

[color=yellow][b]Branching as Possibility:[/b][/color]
[code]
# F[+F][-F]F
#
# F           - draw stem
# [           - SAVE STATE (mark "alternate possibility")
# +F          - turn left, draw branch (explore possibility 1)
# ]           - RESTORE STATE (return to junction)
# [           - SAVE STATE again
# -F          - turn right, draw branch (explore possibility 2)
# ]           - RESTORE STATE
# F           - continue main stem

# The stack holds "roads not taken"
# You can explore, then return to explore differently
[/code]

**The stack is memory of alternate futures** - each [ marks a fork where you could go multiple ways.

**This is non-linear becoming:**
- Not deterministic single path (iterate forward only)
- **Multiple possibilities held simultaneously** (stack stores junctions)
- **Exploration with return** (try branch, come back, try different branch)

**Queer temporality** - you exist in multiple timelines, saved on the stack, to be explored in sequence.

